// case_512_literal_arms  (OPEN compile defect: staged in compile_defects_case_512_arms_addition, see README.md)
//
// A `case` over an int64 with 512 literal arms (0 through 511) and a catch-all. Spec §3.3.3
// (case expressions) and §3.6.4 (pattern compilation) put no limit on the number of case arms; a
// lookup is one flat case with an arm per value. Found in project BEES triage
// (repro bees_triage/arms, 700 arms).
// Today (the stable compiler used for the BEES triage, Mac, 2026-10-23): rejected with E1069
// "function 'id_of' has no parsable body". The same function with 511 literal arms and the
// catch-all compiles and runs correctly (p3 ok / p510 ok / overflow ok / 0), so the limit is
// exactly 512 literal arms.
// Expected:
//   p3 ok
//   p511 ok
//   overflow ok
//   0

